# LINE ENDINGS ARE LF, EVERYWHERE, FOR EVERYBODY.
#
# This repository lives on the WSL filesystem and is worked on from both sides
# of it. Git for Windows is installed with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# text files with CRLF line endings whenever it checks them out. On a Linux tree
# that breaks every shell script outright: bash reads the carriage return as
# part of the interpreter name and fails with "bash\r: No such file or
# directory". The mainnet upgrade is one of those scripts.
#
# Nothing is broken today, because every file here is stored and checked out as
# LF. What was missing is anything stopping the first branch switch, reset or
# stash pop from Windows from changing that. This file does, and because it is
# committed it protects every clone on every platform, which a setting on one
# machine cannot. It overrides core.autocrlf for this repository only.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binary files by content and leave them alone; the
# explicit list below is belt and braces for the binary types this repo holds.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Run by an interpreter that cannot tolerate a carriage return. Stated
# explicitly so they stay LF even if the default above is ever loosened.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary. Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.so binary
